From: =?UTF-8?q?Rouzbeh=E2=80=A0?= <rqzbeh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 10:50:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(server): wire permission_store into app.state

create_app never set app.state.permission_store, so the session-create path
(_validate_session_workspace) always saw is_admin=False for non-owner admins,
yielding 403 'not your host' even with the admin-shared-hosts bypass. Assign
it after agent_store.
---
 omnigent/server/app.py | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/omnigent/server/app.py b/omnigent/server/app.py
index b90d036d6..136d8c8d9 100644
--- a/omnigent/server/app.py
+++ b/omnigent/server/app.py
@@ -1356,6 +1356,7 @@ def create_app(
     app.state.host_registry = host_registry
     app.state.host_store = host_store
     app.state.agent_store = agent_store
+    app.state.permission_store = permission_store
     app.state.sandbox_config = sandbox_config
     app.state.branding_snapshot = branding_snapshot
     app.state.feature_flags = resolved_feature_flags
-- 
